{"productId": "810ce65c-5762-43bc-b1e2-0d200a91369c", "modelName": "1876 Texas Ranger Presidio", "modelDescription": "A bigger better version of the venerable 1873 the 1876 Centennial was built to be a more powerful rifle for the Winchester line. Introduced in 1876 on the centennial of Americas founding and chambered in the whopping 50-95 cartridge the 1876 is an excellent balance of power and capacity. Those looking for a period piece that can still hold its own in the modern day need look no further, with a compact 20 barrel and an 4+1 capacity the 1876 is well equipped to hold its own. A Favorite of frontiersmen the 1876 is a rugged and reliable companion ready for any adventure you take it on. The Texas Ranger Presidio edition has a shorter octagon barrel and reduced magazine tube to make a light and handy saddle ring carbine. Escribed on the receiver is Texas Rangers Co.E- Para muerte de diablos which roughly translates to For death of devils", "manufacturerName": "Cimarron", "subProducts": [{"isFirearm": true, "isNfa": false, "subProductId": "2d917f7b-c950-4b54-830a-8d187cfc0b47", "description": "Cimarron, 1876 Texas Ranger Presidio, Lever Action, 50-95 Winchester, Wood Finish, 20 Barrel, Right Hand, 5 Round Capacity, Iron Sights, Wood Stock", "imageUrls": ["https://main-images.gearfire.com/SubProductImages/e2608add-988c-4ba9-81bd-0dfdca47d9a0"], "isDefault": true, "manufacturerPartNumber": "CA2524", "upc": "844234130078", "attributes": [{"attributeNameId": "4ab35fad-b30f-4bac-b424-1cab633c8b2e", "attributeName": "Threaded", "attributeValueId": "d4d42d7a-e26e-4d65-9450-62ca21c5efa1", "valueName": "No"}, {"attributeNameId": "2765db68-a9f0-406d-8fb7-5b572b01f4ee", "attributeName": "Capacity", "attributeValueId": "89787147-cffc-4da1-8117-39428f54fd75", "valueName": "5 Round"}, {"attributeNameId": "5d7cb225-7607-4efe-ad2f-d56197e694de", "attributeName": "Adjustable Stock", "attributeValueId": "f3810c6c-d0fc-424a-81ad-cfaf1f11ff2f", "valueName": "No"}, {"attributeN